Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:04:35 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 05/27] soc: qcom: ubwc: add SM6225

UBWC 1.0 with the highest bank bit at 14, as on SM6115.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015ya7egg5XM6dMvKwj1kAyq
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/ubwc_config.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/ubwc_config.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/ubwc_config.c
index 23901a4c5..e39c0a5b0 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/ubwc_config.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/ubwc_config.c
@@ -150,6 +150,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id qcom_ubwc_configs[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm4250", .data = &ubwc_1_0_hbb14, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6115", .data = &ubwc_1_0_hbb14, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6125", .data = &ubwc_1_0_hbb14, },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6225", .data = &ubwc_1_0_hbb14, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6150", .data = &ubwc_2_0_hbb14, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6350", .data = &ubwc_2_0_hbb14, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6375", .data = &ubwc_2_0_hbb14, },
